From {{inh|mi|poz-pol-pro|*qaro}} (compare with {{cog|rar|aro}}, {{cog|ty|aro}} and {{cog|sm|alo}}), from {{inh|mi|poz-oce-pro|*qarop}}, from {{inh|mi|poz-pro|*qadəp}} (“front, facing part” – compare with {{cog|jv|ꦲꦉꦥ꧀}} “front, desire”, {{cog|ms|hadap}} “to face”, {{cog|tl|harap}} “front, facade”, {{cog|plw|alep}}).<ref>{{R:Pollex|qaro}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book |page=115 | first = Malcolm D.  | last = Ross | first2=Andrew |last2= Pawley |first3=Meredith |last3=Osmond | year=  2016 | title = The lexicon of Proto-Oceanic | volume = 5: People, body and mind | location = Canberra | publisher = Australian National University | isbn = 9781922185327 }}</ref>

